From 4b9d1ee24f6a5b49106b780d2bc76ef504b9b48c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rautshivamxyz-beep <rautshivamxyz@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:51:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v9.33.147 "A save that returned false is a swallowed failure
 too"

v9.33.90 made NcieFiles.write answer false instead of throwing, which is
the right design - but it silently turned every

    try { NcieFiles.write(f, text) } catch (e: Exception) { NovaLog.quiet(...) }

in the app into dead code. The catch could never run. The false was then
dropped on the floor, because NovaLog.quiet is typed for a Throwable and
there was no Throwable to give it.

So six saves could stop working without a trace anywhere: the growth
report, the capability-gap list, the summary and its count, Jarvis's
trigger mark and its fired-trigger log. All of it is state NOVA reasons
from later, and the health screen - the one place that is supposed to
say "something was swallowed this session" - never heard about any of it.
v9.33.108 and v9.33.111 fixed this exact class by hand in NcieFocus,
NcieExam and NcieTune; these six were the rest of it.

NovaLog gains note(tag, message): the counterpart to quiet() for an
answer instead of an exception. It counts in the same session tally the
health screen reads, records the last one, and cannot throw - it is
called from inside best-effort save paths, where a logging failure would
be worse than the thing being logged.

NcieFiles gains writeOrNote(f, text, tag), which is write() with its
answer recorded when the answer is false. The six sites now ask the one
save function for its answer and let it be heard.

The nightly self-audit was the same bug with a user in front of it: it
wrote its report inside a dead catch and then returned the report, so a
cycle that never reached the disk looked exactly like one that did, and
lastSummary() answered "" next run with nothing explaining why. It now
passes the real answer through reportWithSaveState(), which appends a
plain warning when the report was not saved. The warning never replaces
the report it is warning about.

NovaLogTest pins the record (counted, last-wins, shares one tally with
quiet, and never throws even with the stub android.util.Log a JVM test
runs against); SelfEvolutionEngineTest pins both halves of the report
answer. verify_patches gains nine checks, one of which fails if a dead
try/catch around a save is ever written again - checked against code
lines only, since the fix documents the pattern it removed.

The v9.33.90 invariant that the state files save through NcieFiles now
counts writeOrNote as well: it is a wrapper over the same atomic write,
so the invariant it protects is unchanged.

No inference setting, model weight, permission or network path changed.
